          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, I\u2019ll try eating earlier and smaller meals. How about eating out? I do that a lot\u2014any tips for making better choices at restaurants?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "To make healthier choices when eating out, consider these tips:\n\n1. **Plan Ahead**: Check the restaurant's menu online before you go to identify healthier options. Look for dishes with lean proteins and lots of vegetables.\n\n2. **Choose Wisely**: Opt for grilled, steamed, or baked items instead of fried or creamy dishes. Request sauces and dressings on the side to control how much you use.\n\n3. **Portion Control**: Consider sharing a meal or asking for a smaller portion. You can also eat only half and take the rest home.\n\n4. **Stay Hydrated**: Drink water instead of sugary drinks or alcohol. It helps with digestion and keeps you feeling full.\n\n5. **Be Mindful of Timing**: Eating earlier can help with digestion and reduce reflux symptoms. Aim to finish your meal a few hours before bed.\n\n6. **Speak to Your Server**: Don\u2019t hesitate to ask for modifications or healthier options. Most restaurants are accommodating.\n\nBy implementing these strategies, you can enjoy dining out while making healthier choices that align with your goals.",
