          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "To increase your protein intake while dining out, consider these strategies: \n\n1. **Choose Lean Proteins**: Opt for dishes with lean meats like grilled chicken, turkey, fish, or plant-based proteins such as tofu or legumes. Look for menu items that specify these options.\n\n2. **Add Protein-Rich Sides**: When available, choose sides like beans, lentils, or edamame instead of starchy options like fries or bread.\n\n3. **Breakfast Options**: If you're dining for breakfast, consider egg-based dishes or oatmeal topped with nuts or seeds for added protein.\n\n4. **Modify Your Order**: Don\u2019t hesitate to ask for modifications, like adding extra protein to salads or asking for a protein-rich sauce on the side.\n\n5. **Snack Smart**: If you\u2019re at a caf\u00e9 or bar, look for protein-rich snacks like nuts, cheese, or hummus with veggies.\n\n6. **Check for Healthier Choices**: Many restaurants now indicate healthier options on their menus, including those high in protein. Look for these identifiers.\n\nBy making these choices, you can enjoy your meals out while boosting your protein intake effectively.",
