      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice tips! I actually really love fruits too\u2014especially things like mangoes and pomegranates. Are they good for weight loss or should I avoid them?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "While both mangoes and pomegranates are delicious and nutritious, they have different implications for weight loss. Mangoes are high in sugar, with nearly 31g per fruit, which can be a concern if you're monitoring your sugar intake for weight loss. However, they also provide vitamins A and C and can be enjoyed in moderation. Pomegranates, on the other hand, are lower in calories and high in fiber, which can help you feel full and reduce cravings. They also contain antioxidants that may support weight loss. So, while you can include both in your diet, moderation is key, especially with mangoes. Enjoy them as part of a balanced diet!",
