          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "To handle late-night dinners and work-related stress that may be contributing to your acid reflux, consider these tips:\n\n1. **Plan Your Meals**: Try to have your dinner at least 2-3 hours before bedtime. This can help your body digest food properly and reduce the likelihood of reflux symptoms.\n\n2. **Choose Lighter Meals**: Opt for lighter, balanced meals in the evening, focusing on lean proteins, vegetables, and whole grains. Avoid heavy, spicy, or fatty foods that can trigger reflux.\n\n3. **Practice Relaxation Techniques**: Incorporate stress management strategies such as deep breathing, meditation, or gentle yoga in the evening to help reduce stress levels before bed.\n\n4. **Create a Wind-Down Routine**: Establish a calming pre-sleep routine that allows you to relax and disconnect from work-related stress. This can include reading, listening to music, or taking a warm bath.\n\n5. **Limit Screen Time**: Reduce screen time before bed to help your mind unwind. Consider setting a cut-off time for work-related emails or messages.\n\n6. **Stay Hydrated**: Drink water throughout the",
