          "user_utterance": "Thanks! Meal ideas with more protein would be great. I want to switch things up from my usual late-night takeout. Any suggestions, especially with fruits I enjoy?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For high-protein, late-night dinners, consider dishes like grilled chicken or tofu served with quinoa and a salsa made from mango, pomegranate, and fresh herbs. You can also try a protein-rich apple oatmeal, which is quick to prepare and filling [clueweb22-en0004-06-10562:5]. Meal prepping is key: roast several servings of your favorite proteins and prepare grains like quinoa or rice in advance, then pair them with pre-chopped fruits such as apples, mangoes, or watermelon for easy, healthy meals [clueweb22-en0001-82-18279:9]. When eating out, choose meals similar to what you'd make at home and swap heavy sides for salads or extra veggies to keep your protein intake high and calories in check. For more variety, explore high-protein dinner recipes that include lean meats, legumes, or plant-based proteins, and incorporate your favorite fruits as sides or toppings [clueweb22-en0005-04-09330:0]. Would you like specific recipes using mango or pomegranate?",
          "citations": {
