          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a have better psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "For a quick, high-protein vegetarian meal, make a Cold Chopped Quinoa Salad with Eggs and Pomegranate. Cook quinoa and let it cool. Chop carrots, cucumbers, and parsley, then mix with the quinoa and pomegranate arils. Add hard-boiled eggs (sliced or chopped) for protein. Dress with olive oil, lemon juice, salt, and pepper. This meal is gluten-free, filling, and perfect for meal prep, taking less than 30 minutes to prepare [clueweb22-en0031-61-18629:7][clueweb22-en0021-77-17936:11]. To reduce the urge to check your phone while cooking or eating, place your phone in another room or use 'Do Not Disturb' mode. Try setting a specific intention before meals (like enjoying the flavors or reflecting on your day), and consider using a physical book or music for background entertainment instead of your phone. These strategies help break the habit and make meals more mindful. Would you like more quick vegetarian recipes with different fruits?",
