          "user_utterance": "Yes, meal prep strategies would help. Anything simple for someone who eats out a lot and is always short on time?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "To make meal prep work with a busy lifestyle and frequent dining out, start by prepping a few core ingredients\u2014such as cooked quinoa, beans, or hard-boiled eggs\u2014that can be quickly combined with fresh or pre-chopped fruits and vegetables for high-protein, nutritious meals [clueweb22-en0013-39-17536:0]. Batch-cook grains and proteins once or twice a week, and store them in the fridge for easy access. Choose simple recipes with 10 ingredients or less to avoid feeling overwhelmed, and don't aim for perfection\u2014just prepping a couple of meals can make a big difference [clueweb22-en0038-87-08565:5]. Plan your meal prep around your social life: if you know you'll eat out several times, prep only for the nights you\u2019ll be home, so you don\u2019t waste food or effort [clueweb22-en0028-31-10844:2]. This flexible approach helps you eat healthier without giving up your favorite restaurants or feeling pressured to cook every night.",
