      {
        "turn": 10,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That sounds doable, thanks! Any suggestions for making healthy choices when eating out, like at a local pizzeria or similar places?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "When eating out at a pizzeria, opt for a thin and crispy crust or even a veggie-based crust like cauliflower to reduce calories [clueweb22-en0035-17-15532:0]. Choose toppings such as turkey pepperoni, grilled chicken, or extra veggies to boost protein and fiber while keeping calories in check. Go easy on cheese and avoid fatty or fried toppings. If you eat late, try to avoid heavy, fatty, or acidic foods (like extra tomato sauce) to minimize discomfort and support better digestion [clueweb22-en0036-65-05290:11]. For a balanced meal, aim for at least 25\u201330g of protein by adding lean animal or plant-based proteins to your pizza or side salad [clueweb22-en0030-57-08287:12]. Would you like ideas for healthy side dishes to pair with pizza?",
