      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, please! I always eat dinner late and want it to be healthier, with more protein. Any suggestions?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "When eating dinner late and aiming for more protein, focus on meals that are light yet filling. Great choices include grilled or baked chicken, fish, or tofu, as well as Greek yogurt or cottage cheese, which provide slow-release protein to support muscle repair overnight [clueweb22-en0045-08-06817]. Pairing these proteins with fiber-rich vegetables or a salad can help you feel satisfied without being overly full, and also supports digestive health [clueweb22-en0014-57-11581]. If you're dining out, look for menu items that are grilled or steamed, and don't hesitate to ask for extra veggies instead of heavier sides. Plant-based protein options or protein-rich salads are also excellent, especially if you want something lighter. These choices can help you manage weight and support your goal of increasing protein intake, even with a late-night schedule [clueweb22-en0005-04-09330]. Are you interested in portable, protein-rich snacks for late nights?",
