      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Not right now, but that\u2019s interesting. Changing the topic, is it true that sitting for long periods makes it hard to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Prolonged sitting is associated with higher levels of abdominal fat and can make weight loss more difficult because it reduces your overall daily energy expenditure [clueweb22-en0039-75-11364]. Studies show that taking more breaks from sitting, even very short ones, is linked to better glucose and lipid levels and decreased body fat [clueweb22-en0033-75-09446]. While simply standing instead of sitting doesn't burn a lot more calories, incorporating more movement throughout your day\u2014like walking during calls or using the stairs\u2014can add up and help counteract the effects of a sedentary lifestyle [clueweb22-en0021-95-08339][clueweb22-en0033-75-09446]. For someone with a desk job, making small adjustments to move more often is key to supporting weight loss and overall health. Are standing desks effective for weight loss?",
