          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that helps! I think putting it on my calendar could work. What about healthy food choices when eating out? I eat out often.",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "To make healthier choices when dining out, look for menu items that are grilled, baked, or steamed rather than fried or creamed, and avoid dishes with heavy sauces [clueweb22-en0000-47-06308]. Ask for salad dressings and sauces on the side so you can control the amount, and request substitutions like extra vegetables instead of fries [clueweb22-en0019-39-07419]. Opt for water or unsweetened beverages, and try to include lean protein sources such as grilled chicken, fish, or plant-based proteins in your meal [clueweb22-en0028-30-03115]. If you eat late at night, lighter meals with vegetables and protein can help you feel satisfied without being overly heavy. Many restaurants are open to special requests, so don't hesitate to ask for modifications that align with your health goals [clueweb22-en0019-39-07419]. Do you want advice on healthy late-night dining options?",
