      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful. Is there a link between stomach acid reflux and psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Scientific studies confirm a bidirectional association between acid reflux (GERD) and psychological health. Stress and anxiety can worsen acid reflux symptoms by affecting gut motility and lowering the pressure at the esophagus-stomach junction, which can trigger or intensify reflux episodes. Conversely, persistent acid reflux symptoms can contribute to the development of depression and anxiety, creating a cycle where each condition exacerbates the other. Patients with GERD who also experience depression or anxiety often report more severe symptoms and a lower quality of life, even if their physical reflux parameters are similar to those without mental health issues. Addressing both psychological and physical aspects is important for effective management of GERD and overall well-being [clueweb22-en0002-65-07759][clueweb22-en0032-63-09386]. Are there dietary changes that can support both gut and mental health?",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0002-65-07759:15": 0.05557781073899299,
            "clueweb22-en0002-65-07759:12": 0.048856704550610225,
            "clueweb22-en0002-65-07759:13": 0.046871392288155164,
