          "text": "To manage cravings and indulgences while increasing protein and eating out, use these targeted strategies:\n\n**1. Don\u2019t Restrict\u2014Plan for Treats**\n- Allow yourself occasional indulgences. Viewing healthy eating as a long-term lifestyle, not a strict rule, prevents feelings of deprivation and rebound overeating ([clueweb22-en0004-04-06955], [clueweb22-en0013-96-08438]).\n- Mindfully enjoy your favorite foods in moderation, especially when dining out.\n\n**2. Prioritize Protein to Curb Cravings**\n- High-protein meals and snacks (lean meats, eggs, Greek yogurt, beans, tofu) help you feel full and reduce cravings for sweets and salty foods ([clueweb22-en0036-14-18244], [clueweb22-en0011-31-11693]).\n- Start meals with protein to stabilize blood sugar and appetite.\n\n**3. Find Healthier Alternatives**\n- Swap typical indulgences for protein-rich or nutrient-dense versions (e.g., protein bars, roasted chickpeas, fruit",
