          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 1,
          "text": "Given your goals\u2014higher protein intake, frequent dining out, recent weight gain, and a desire for sustainable lifestyle change\u2014here are the most relevant health conditions and risks to be aware of:\n\n**1. Weight-Related Risks**\n- **Obesity** increases your risk for heart disease, type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, and certain cancers ([clueweb22-en0004-86-05045], [clueweb22-en0034-09-00524]).\n- Recent inactivity can also contribute to metabolic syndrome and worsen acid reflux (GERD).\n\n**2. Digestive Health**\n- **Acid Reflux (GERD):** More common with weight gain, inactivity, and stress. Eating large or fatty meals, alcohol, and certain foods (spicy, chocolate, caffeine) can trigger symptoms ([clueweb22-en0001-00-11310], [clueweb22-en0035-62-03918]).\n- **Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS):** Can be aggravated by dietary changes and stress ([clueweb22",
