          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That makes sense, but can you be more specific? What small changes should I start with, especially if I want to be more active and eat better?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to get started to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To start with, you can try incorporating small amounts of physical activity into your daily routine, such as taking a short walk each day or doing a few jumping jacks during commercial breaks while watching TV. For eating better, you can start by making small changes like choosing healthy snacks, such as nuts or fruits, instead of unhealthy ones. You can also try to cook at home more often and prepare meals in advance to ensure you're eating nutritious food. Remember, the key is to make small, achievable changes that you can stick to in the long term, rather than trying to make drastic changes that may be hard to maintain.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0028-79-14842:1": 5.293649673461914,
            "clueweb22-en0017-72-14196:3": 5.138426780700684,
            "clueweb22-en0017-72-14196:4": 4.282863140106201,
            "clueweb22-en0019-30-10147:0": 4.093131065368652,
            "clueweb22-en0020-95-03546:2": 4.0289835929870605
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Got it! I eat out a lot and usually walk very little. Any tips for eating out healthier, and how to stay active when I'm busy with work?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "When eating out, try to choose restaurants that offer healthy options and opt for smaller portions. You can also consider packing your own lunch or snacks to avoid relying on fast food or unhealthy takeout. To stay active, find ways to incorporate physical activity into your daily routine, such as taking the stairs instead of the elevator or going for a short walk during your breaks. Even small amounts of exercise, like a 10-minute walk, can make a big difference. Additionally, consider meal prepping or cooking at home when you have time, so you have healthy meals ready to go on busy days. This can help you avoid relying on unhealthy convenience foods and ensure you're getting the nutrients you need to stay energized and focused.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0033-11-07552:13": 5.399785041809082,
            "clueweb22-en0024-30-04362:3": 4.9561357498168945,
            "clueweb22-en0007-31-04403:0": 4.762355327606201,
            "clueweb22-en0039-49-02692:13": 4.538592338562012,
            "clueweb22-en0000-25-01097:0": 4.350523471832275
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! My work as a software engineer keeps me at my desk a lot, and I tend to doom scroll during breaks. Any ideas for better habits that might help my mental health?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a have better psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "As a software engineer, it's great that you're recognizing the need to break the habit of doom scrolling. Consider using your breaks to stretch, move around, or practice mindfulness meditation. You can also set time restrictions on your social media apps to limit your screen time. Additionally, try to prioritize self-care activities, such as taking a short walk or doing some light exercise, to help reduce stress and improve your mental well-being. By making these small changes, you can develop healthier habits that will benefit your mental health and overall quality of life.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.   (",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0033-80-18878:12": 0.48502880334854126,
            "clueweb22-en0044-71-15204:14": -2.1932592391967773,
            "clueweb22-en0012-72-02602:10": -2.266547679901123,
            "clueweb22-en0038-79-11657:10": -2.4183993339538574,
            "clueweb22-en0034-54-08337:17": -2.4217207431793213
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful. Another thing I\u2019ve been wondering: is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there is a connection between stomach acid reflux and psychological health. Research has shown that people with anxiety and depression are more likely to experience acid reflux symptoms. This is because stress and anxiety can affect the digestive system, leading to an imbalance in gut bacteria and increased inflammation, which can contribute to acid reflux. Additionally, some studies suggest that the gut and brain are connected, and that psychological stress can affect the functioning of the digestive system, leading to symptoms like acid reflux. So, managing stress and anxiety through techniques like mindfulness, exercise, and therapy may also help alleviate acid reflux symptoms.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0029-53-12907:11": 3.8040695190429688,
            "clueweb22-en0019-00-09018:7": 3.751473903656006,
            "clueweb22-en0008-36-04281:1": 3.7304441928863525,
            "clueweb22-en0021-39-19846:0": 3.3673605918884277,
            "clueweb22-en0044-75-01522:0": 2.4305543899536133
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really interesting. I guess I need to address my phone usage and late-night eating, too. How bad is eating late for weight loss?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Eating late at night can be detrimental to your weight loss efforts. When you eat late, your body is more likely to store the calories as fat, rather than using them for energy. This is because your body's natural rhythm is designed for rest and repair at night, and eating can disrupt this process. Additionally, late-night eating can also affect your metabolic health, increasing your risk of insulin resistance, pre-diabetes, and other health issues. It's best to try to avoid eating late at night and instead focus on eating a balanced diet during the day to support your weight loss goals.   Please let me know if I can assist you further.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-15-12738:2": 8.693488121032715,
            "clueweb22-en0031-68-05276:5": 8.14874267578125,
            "clueweb22-en0040-49-18596:6": 7.621867656707764,
            "clueweb22-en0015-16-16169:5": 7.234274387359619,
            "clueweb22-en0013-15-12738:3": 7.18665885925293
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! I actually always eat dinner pretty late because of my work schedule. Any suggestions for healthy late-night meals or snacks?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Eating a late dinner can be challenging, but there are healthy options you can consider. For a late-night meal, try to opt for something light and balanced, such as a small portion of lean protein, vegetables, and whole grains. Some examples include a small serving of grilled chicken or fish with roasted vegetables, or a bowl of oatmeal with fruit and nuts. If you need a snack, choose something nutritious like non-fat milk, whole fruits, or a handful of nuts. Avoid heavy, greasy, or high-calorie foods that can disrupt your sleep and hinder your weight loss efforts. Also, be mindful of your portion sizes to maintain a healthy balance.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0037-72-06502:0": 6.148016929626465,
            "clueweb22-en0014-51-02287:14": 5.987761497497559,
            "clueweb22-en0044-59-10821:19": 5.331394195556641,
            "clueweb22-en0036-65-05290:11": 5.320915222167969,
            "clueweb22-en0022-07-14157:7": 4.893717288970947
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s great advice. I love fruits, especially kiwi, watermelon, and lately fresh mangoes. Are there specific fruits that are particularly good for weight loss?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "Kiwi, watermelon, and mangoes are all great choices for weight loss. Kiwi is high in fiber and low in calories, making it a great snack for weight loss. Watermelon is also low in calories and high in water content, which can help with hydration and weight loss. Mangoes are rich in vitamins and minerals, and they're also relatively low in calories. Other fruits that are good for weight loss include berries, such as blueberries and strawberries, which are high in antioxidants and fiber. Figs are also a good option, as they're low in calories and high in fiber, which can help with digestion and weight loss. Overall, incorporating a variety of fruits into your diet can help support your weight loss goals.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0003-90-08314:3": 4.143712043762207,
            "clueweb22-en0041-45-11666:16": 4.0992584228515625,
