        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 9,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great advice\u2014turning off phone notifications sounds doable. I\u2019ve also thought about doing an internet detox. What\u2019s the best way to start one without feeling too isolated?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To start an internet detox without feeling isolated, consider setting boundaries and making it work for your life and demands. You don't have to completely separate from your phone and other tech connections. Try doing a mini-detox, like turning off devices at the end of the workday and focusing on spending an evening free of social media, texting, and online videos. You can also schedule time with friends or family, or engage in activities like reading, walking, or sports to fill the time. This way, you can benefit from the detox without feeling cut off from the world. Start small and be realistic, and you'll find it more manageable.",
