          "text": "To break the habit of spending too much time on your phone, especially late at night, try setting a specific time to put your phone away before bed. You can also establish a bedtime routine that doesn't involve screens, such as reading a book or taking a warm bath. Another strategy is to turn off notifications for non-essential apps and use features like screen time tracking to monitor your phone usage. Additionally, consider implementing a \"no phone\" policy during certain hours of the day or in specific locations, like the dinner table. By making these small changes, you can start to reduce your phone usage and improve your overall well-being.",
