        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019ve actually been eating dinner pretty late at night, so that probably doesn\u2019t help! How can I fit exercise into a busy schedule, like when you work full-time at a desk job?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To fit exercise into a busy full-time desk job schedule, integrate movement throughout your workday. Take stairs instead of elevators, and park farther away to add steps. Utilize your lunch break for a brisk walk or gym session. At your desk, incorporate simple exercises like leg lifts, stretches, or standing push-ups, or consider a standing desk or under-desk elliptical. Get up and move around for 5-10 minutes every hour. For more intense workouts, try efficient options like HIIT or weight training, or exercise first thing in the morning.",
