        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Good reminder\u2014I should reconnect with friends. Is stomach acid reflux connected to how stressed or anxious I feel?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there's a strong mind-body connection. Stress and anxiety can worsen acid reflux by affecting digestion, relaxing the lower esophageal sphincter (LES), and potentially increasing stomach acid. They can also make you more sensitive to pain, making heartburn feel more severe. This creates a cycle where reflux can also trigger anxiety.",
