      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! Can more protein help with psychological health too?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a have better psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 2,
          "text": "Yes, increased protein intake can potentially benefit psychological health. Studies suggest that high protein intake is protectively associated with severe depressive symptoms and a lower prevalence of mental illnesses. Protein can influence brain function and mental health by producing neurotransmitters and promoting greater satiety, which may lead to a better mood and reduced irritability. Additionally, adequate protein supports growth hormone levels, which are linked to preventing various psychological issues.",
