      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s helpful. Is there a link between psychological health and stomach acid reflux?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there's a significant link between psychological health, particularly stress and anxiety, and stomach acid reflux. Stress doesn't always increase stomach acid, but it can heighten your sensitivity to it, making reflux symptoms feel worse and more uncomfortable. There's also a bidirectional relationship: stress can trigger or worsen reflux, and persistent reflux symptoms can, in turn, contribute to anxiety and depression, creating a cycle. Managing stress through lifestyle changes can be key to managing reflux symptoms.",
