        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That helps! I eat out most days\u2014any tips for making healthier choices at restaurants?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "When dining out, opt for grilled, baked, or steamed dishes instead of fried. Choose lean proteins like skinless chicken, turkey, or fish to increase intake and manage weight. For acid reflux, avoid high-fat foods, creamy sauces, and acidic ingredients like tomatoes, raw onions, and citrus. Request non-spicy versions. For salads, choose low-fat dressings and add lean protein. Opt for broth-based soups or steamed dishes at Asian restaurants.",
