      {
        "turn": 9,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Great advice. I definitely need to move more. If I\u2019ve gained weight after not exercising for months, what\u2019s a realistic way to start getting active again?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "To realistically restart activity after a break and weight gain, begin slowly and set small, achievable goals. Don't aim for daily intense workouts immediately. Instead, incorporate short bouts of activity, like 10-15 minute walks or taking the stairs, and gradually increase duration and intensity. Find activities you enjoy to maintain consistency. Consider consulting a doctor, especially if you have concerns, as even small changes add up.",
