        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Very helpful, thanks! I\u2019ve heard psychological health might affect stomach acid reflux\u2014are the two related?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there's a strong, often bidirectional, relationship between psychological health and stomach acid reflux. Stress, anxiety, and depression can worsen acid reflux symptoms or increase your sensitivity to the pain, potentially by affecting stomach acid production or pain perception. Conversely, chronic acid reflux can be a stressful experience, which may trigger or aggravate anxiety and depression. This creates a cycle where mental and physical discomfort can feed off each other.",
