        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks! I love reading Stephen King, so I\u2019ll definitely pick up a book. What about dietary swaps for someone who likes eating out, especially at pizzerias?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "For pizzerias, opt for a whole wheat crust and choose white, pesto, or olive oil-based sauces instead of tomato. Load up on lean protein toppings like chicken or turkey, and plenty of vegetables such as spinach, mushrooms, or green peppers. Request lean or low-fat cheese. When eating out generally, ask for lean meats grilled, steamed, or roasted instead of fried. Swap fries for a side salad or steamed vegetables, and request sauces on the side to control portions. Focus on lean proteins like chicken, fish, tofu, or legumes to boost your intake.",
