          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Nice, thanks! What about small exercise habits? I work as a software engineer, so I sit most of the day. Any routine that isn\u2019t overwhelming?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "To integrate small, non-overwhelming exercise habits into your day as a software engineer, focus on consistent movement. Set a reminder to get up and stretch every 30-60 minutes, incorporating simple desk exercises like calf raises, chair squats, or neck and shoulder stretches. Increase incidental movement by taking the stairs, walking to colleagues instead of messaging, or going for a short walk during your lunch break. Staying well-hydrated also helps, as it encourages more frequent trips to the water cooler or restroom. Even 5-10 minute bursts of activity can significantly improve your well-being.",
