      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I\u2019ll try the no-eating-after-dinner rule. I do get bored and snack while doom scrolling on my phone. Any suggestions for cutting down on phone time, too?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "To cut down on phone time and doom scrolling, especially when bored, try these strategies. Adjust your phone settings: change your screen to grayscale, turn off unnecessary notifications, and use screen time limits or app-blocking features. Create physical distance by keeping your phone out of your bedroom or in another room. Also, replace phone time with engaging activities. Sign up for a class, pursue a hobby, or make phone-free plans like a hike or spending time with friends. You can also position healthy apps (like meditation or language learning) next to social media apps for a positive alternative.",
