        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, that makes sense. Actually, is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health in any way?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes, there's a strong and often bidirectional relationship between stomach acid reflux and psychological health.\n\nStress, anxiety, and depression can trigger or worsen acid reflux symptoms by affecting stomach acid production, relaxing the lower esophageal sphincter, or increasing sensitivity to pain. Conversely, persistent acid reflux symptoms can contribute to or exacerbate anxiety and depression. This connection is largely due to the \"gut-brain axis,\" where the digestive system and brain are intimately linked.",
