    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I want to start living healthier and be more active, but not sure where to begin. Any tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to get started to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "great place to start \u2014 keep it simple and consistent. - move most days : 10 \u2013 20 minute brisk walk after meals ( especially dinner ) and 2 short strength sessions / week ( push - ups, squats, rows, planks ). gradually add time / sets. - at work : pomodoro breaks, stretch every hour, take stairs, short walking meetings. bike / walk or use transit when possible to cut co2. - protein at every meal / snack ( goal ~ 20 \u2013 40 g ) : baked egg cups or greek yogurt chia bowls for breakfast ; grain / greens bowl with legumes, fish, or poultry for lunch. snacks : greek yogurt and berries, apple + peanut butter, cottage cheese, hummus with veggies, boiled eggs, tuna / salmon packets, chia pudding, or a protein smoothie. - enjoy fruit variety ( mango, pomegranate, kiwi, watermelon ) \u2014 pair with yogurt / cottage cheese or nuts to stay full. - late dinners : keep them lighter \u2014 protein + veggies or a smoothie ; aim to stop eating 2 \u2013 3 hours before bed when you can. - eat out : choose grilled",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0037-08-13439:0": -0.43624255061149597,
            "clueweb22-en0001-67-10451:2": -0.5143951773643494,
            "clueweb22-en0017-83-16530:1": -0.5374665260314941,
            "clueweb22-en0029-89-03176:15": -0.5490548610687256,
            "clueweb22-en0043-08-14553:13": -0.5796785950660706
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s super helpful! I definitely eat dinner late and tend to eat out a lot\u2014sometimes at my local pizzeria. Any practical ideas for making eating out healthier, especially at places like pizza spots?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 3,
          "text": "absolutely \u2014 here \u2019 s a simple playbook for pizza nights and eating out : before you go - don \u2019 t arrive starving : have a small protein snack ( greek yogurt, boiled egg, handful of nuts ). - scan the menu online and pre - pick your order ; track it in your food journal / app. at pizza spots - choose thin - crust / neapolitan ; whole \u2011 wheat if available. ask for light cheese and extra tomato sauce. - load veggies ( peppers, mushrooms, onions, spinach, arugula ). add lean protein : grilled chicken, shrimp, or anchovies. - skip / limit high - cal meats ( pepperoni / sausage ), stuffed or pan crusts, and creamy / cheesy dips. - portion control : personal pie or 1 \u2013 2 slices ; box half upfront or split with a friend. - start with a big side salad ( oil & vinegar on the side ). add grilled chicken for protein. - drinks : water or unsweetened tea ; avoid sugary drinks and keep alcohol modest. late dinners - go lighter : 1 slice + salad or minestrone. if sleep is near, take a 10 \u2013",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0040-11-11392:1": -2.7935986518859863,
            "clueweb22-en0042-60-00493:4": -3.080183982849121,
            "clueweb22-en0004-69-03742:6": -3.4661617279052734,
            "clueweb22-en0008-50-10590:7": -3.828418493270874,
            "clueweb22-en0035-11-17702:8": -3.8836898803710938
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s really practical, thanks! I love veggie-loaded pizzas and can definitely try lighter options. About those late dinners\u2014sometimes I eat right before bed because of work. Any tips to avoid this, since I\u2019m often coding late at night?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "totally doable, even with late - night coding. try these : - split dinner : eat a solid, protein - forward meal earlier ( 5 \u2013 7 pm ), then if you \u2019 re still up late, have a small, light snack 1 \u2013 2 hours before bed. - set a \u201c kitchen curfew \u201d 2 \u2013 3 hours before sleep. put a reminder before you start your evening coding sprint. - pre - prep \u201c code fuel \u201d so you don \u2019 t default to big meals : greek yogurt or cottage cheese with mango / pomegranate / kiwi, chia pudding, lentil soup, tofu + veggies, hummus with veggies, a boiled egg, or a small smoothie ( greek yogurt or soy milk, spinach, fruit ). keep portions light and lower - fat for easier digestion. - if pizza is unavoidable late : 1 slice max + big salad, then a 10 \u2013 15 minute walk to aid digestion ; save extra for lunch. - cut caffeine 6 \u2013 8 hours before bed ; switch to water or herbal tea. - use pomodoro blocks to schedule an earlier meal break ; hydrate first and wait 20",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-25-16998:6": -2.4748387336730957,
            "clueweb22-en0013-25-16998:5": -2.816652297973633,
            "clueweb22-en0021-11-12310:7": -3.967740058898926,
            "clueweb22-en0045-89-08458:17": -4.091485500335693,
            "clueweb22-en0018-36-12632:7": -4.281024932861328
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s great advice! I\u2019ll try splitting dinner and prepping snacks ahead of time\u2014fresh fruit and yogurt sounds perfect. Any ideas for making my workspace better for mental health, especially since I spend long hours at the computer?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a have better psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "love that plan. here are workspace tweaks that support mental health during long coding sessions : - ergonomics : chair with lumbar support, monitor at eye level, wrists neutral. consider a split / ergonomic keyboard and external mouse ; alternate sitting / standing ( e. g., 45 / 15 ). - microbreaks : pomodoro ( 25 / 5 or 50 / 10 ). every hour, stand, stretch, or take a 5 \u2013 10 min walk \u2014 great after late - night work to decompress. - eyes : 20 - 20 - 20 rule ; blink often. use night light / blue \u2011 shift on your devices in the evening. keep room lighting warm and dim at night. - noise and focus : use noise - cancelling or brown noise. turn off nonessential notifications ; on android use focus mode / bedtime mode and app timers. keep your phone out of reach while coding. - boundaries : set a \u201c shutdown ritual \u201d ( save, plan tomorrow \u2019 s top 3, clear desk ). aim to stop heavy work 30 \u2013 60 min before sleep. - mood boosters : add a plant, natural light, and water bottle. keep prepped \u201c",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0030-29-09211:5": -2.7454941272735596,
            "clueweb22-en0036-13-09373:2": -4.9087934494018555,
            "clueweb22-en0025-70-06725:6": -5.119551658630371,
            "clueweb22-en0022-99-11073:0": -5.242666244506836,
            "clueweb22-en0036-18-10993:1": -5.391014099121094
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Awesome! I\u2019ll set up a shutdown ritual and try app timers\u2014my screen time is honestly too high. Is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health, like stress or anxiety?",
          "user_rubrik": "Is stomach acid reflux related to psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "short answer : yes. stress and anxiety don \u2019 t \u201c cause \u201d gerd on their own, but they can : - increase symptom perception ( you feel heartburn more intensely ) - trigger behaviors that worsen reflux ( late, larger, faster meals ; more caffeine / alcohol ) - sometimes increase reflux episodes via more frequent les relaxations what helps : - diaphragmatic breathing 5 \u2013 10 minutes after meals and before bed ( inhale 4 sec, exhale 6 \u2013 8 sec ). it can reduce reflux episodes and calms anxiety. - microbreak walks and light post \u2011 meal walks ( 10 \u2013 15 minutes ). - split dinner : earlier protein \u2011 forward meal, then a small, low \u2011 fat snack if you must work late. - eat slowly ; stop 2 \u2013 3 hours before sleep when possible. if not, keep it small and low \u2011 fat. - sleep with the head of the bed elevated and on your left side. - cut caffeine 6 \u2013 8 hours before bed ; avoid mint, alcohol, and carbonated drinks late. - screen \u2011 time hygiene : your shutdown ritual, focus / bedtime mode, app timers, and keeping the phone out of reach. see",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0005-44-06345:0": -5.370852470397949,
            "clueweb22-en0005-44-06345:1": -6.847402095794678,
            "clueweb22-en0008-35-17474:8": -6.852729797363281,
            "clueweb22-en0018-35-17756:4": -7.341124057769775,
            "clueweb22-en0037-51-11247:11": -7.584067344665527
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 6,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks. The breathing technique sounds doable. Since I stopped working out, I\u2019ve felt more tired and gained weight. How should I start exercising again if I don\u2019t want to overdo it?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 4,
          "text": "great call easing back in. here \u2019 s a simple, low \u2011 stress restart plan : weeks 1 \u2013 2 - move most days : 10 \u2013 15 minute brisk walk after meals ( great for reflux, energy ). - strength 2x / week, 20 minutes. do 2 sets of 8 \u2013 12 reps, leaving 2 \u2013 3 reps in reserve : - squat ( bodyweight or goblet ) - incline push \u2011 ups - bent \u2011 over row ( db / backpack ) - hip hinge / rdl ( light dbs ) - plank 2\u00d720 \u2013 40s - warm up 5 minutes ( easy walk + joint circles ). cool down with 2 \u2013 3 minutes diaphragmatic breathing. weeks 3 \u2013 4 - add a 3rd strength day or extend walks to 20 \u2013 30 minutes. - optional : 1 short interval session ( 5 \u2013 10 min : 30s easy / 30s brisk on a bike or walk hills ). progression - add 1 rep or a little weight each week ; or 1 extra set after week 2. - if soreness lasts > 48 hours or sleep / energy dip, scale back 10 \u2013 20 %. - every 4th week, keep volume lighter ( deload ). recovery and habits -",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0028-87-08045:6": -1.4444119930267334,
            "clueweb22-en0026-47-01644:6": -1.6637141704559326,
            "clueweb22-en0026-47-01644:7": -1.9382280111312866,
            "clueweb22-en0006-27-14428:1": -2.1469614505767822,
            "clueweb22-en0021-49-16704:0": -2.182995557785034
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That progression sounds manageable\u2014thank you! I have a question about metabolism. What are some spices that can help boost metabolism?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some spices that can help boost metabolism?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "short version : spices can give a small metabolic nudge, but the big wins still come from protein, fiber, steps, and sleep. good options and how to use them : - chili / cayenne ( capsaicin ) : increases thermogenesis and fat oxidation. try 1 / 8 \u2013 1 / 2 tsp in bean bowls or on veggie pizza. note : can aggravate reflux \u2014 avoid late at night if sensitive. - ginger : mild thermogenic and appetite benefits. aim 1 \u2013 2 g / day ( fresh or powdered ) in smoothies or stir \u2011 fries. - cinnamon ( prefer ceylon ) : may improve insulin sensitivity and post \u2011 meal glucose. 1 / 2 \u2013 1 tsp on greek yogurt with mango / pomegranate or in oats. - turmeric + black pepper : supports insulin sensitivity and recovery ; pepper ( piperine ) boosts absorption. 1 / 2 \u2013 1 tsp turmeric with a pinch of pepper in lentils, eggs, or a golden milk made with soy milk. - cumin : small studies show modest weight benefits. 1 / 2 \u2013 1 tsp in chickpeas, couscous, or soups.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0009-26-18845:1": -1.3124135732650757,
            "clueweb22-en0029-10-09297:3": -2.845392942428589,
