          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "You don\u2019t need to panic\u2014small, consistent steps can reverse recent weight gain and improve fitness and sleep. Key points to start today:  - Move daily: 20\u201330 minutes brisk walk or sprinkle 3\u20135 minute micro\u2011workouts through the day.   - Add strength 2\u20133\u00d7/week (bodyweight squats, push\u2011ups, planks, lunges) \u2014 builds muscle and boosts metabolism.   - Fix one meal: swap one dinner for lean protein + veggies/whole grain. Small food changes matter more than perfection.   - Tackle timing: finish eating 2\u20133 hours before bed; try moving dinner 15\u201330 minutes earlier each week.   - Progress slowly: add 1 extra minute, 1 rep, or 1 healthy swap per week to keep it sustainable.   - Accountability: buddy, app, or short weekly check\u2011ins help you stick with it.   - Expect gradual wins: better sleep and endurance show up in weeks; noticeable weight change in months.   If you have medical concerns or big weight changes, check with your clinician.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-71-14353:5": 38.452999114990234,
            "clueweb22-en0031-42-11189:5": 38.452999114990234,
