      {
        "turn": 8,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Feeling better already! Shifting gears\u2014are there spices or foods that can help with metabolism?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some spices that can help boost metabolism?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Yes \u2014 some foods and spices can give a small metabolic lift, but the biggest effects come from activity and more muscle. Practical picks:  - Protein: lean meats, eggs, dairy, beans \u2014 higher \u201cthermic effect\u201d (your body burns more to digest protein) and helps preserve/build muscle.   - Spicy peppers (capsaicin): can modestly raise calorie burn and reduce appetite for some people.   - Coffee and green tea: caffeine (and green tea catechins) can slightly increase metabolism and alertness \u2014 use in moderation.   - Fiber-rich whole foods: vegetables, whole grains, and legumes support digestion and stable blood sugar.   - Probiotics/prebiotics: promising for metabolic health, but effects are strain-specific and not guaranteed.  Avoid quick-fix \u201cmetabolism\u201d teas or laxative blends \u2014 evidence is limited and some ingredients (senna, certain herbal mixes, excess licorice) can cause harm. Biggest wins: add protein to meals, use a bit of chili or green tea if you like, and combine with daily movement plus 2\u20133 strength sessions per week.",
