            "clueweb22-en0045-01-06850:1": 46.657100677490234
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 3,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "That\u2019s practical, thanks! I usually eat out, mostly pizza from a local place and sometimes heavy stuff. Any smart tricks to make eating out healthier, especially for protein?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Great \u2014 practical, tasty ideas you can use right away:  - Pick the protein first: order grilled/steamed/roasted proteins (chicken breast, turkey, fish, tofu, shrimp) rather than fried or breaded. - Ask for sauces on the side and \u201clight oil\u201d or \u201cno added salt\u201d to cut calories and sodium. - Double up on veggies: swap fries/rice for extra veggies or a side salad. - For pizza: choose thin crust, tomato base, lean toppings (grilled chicken, veggies), and skip extra cheese or ask for less. - Share or portion control: split an entr\u00e9e or box half before you eat so you don\u2019t overeat. - Lean swaps: brown rice/quinoa instead of white rice or noodles when possible. - Time it: eat a small veggie or piece of fruit before you go out to reduce overeating. - Bring a backup protein: a protein bar or a small cooked chicken breast works if options are limited. - Simple rule: if the dish is mostly protein + veggies with a light sauce, it\u2019s usually the healthier pick.  Want quick sample orders for pizza, Chinese, or fast-casual places?",
          "citations": {
