      {
        "turn": 4,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Yes, sample \u201chealthier\u201d orders for pizza and Chinese would be great! Oh, and if you have a simple protein snack idea for work, that\u2019d help too.",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a have better psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Great \u2014 quick, practical picks:  Pizza - Thin crust with tomato base, ask for light cheese or half the usual amount.   - Lean toppings: grilled chicken, shrimp, mushrooms, spinach, peppers, onions.   - Skip pepperoni/extra cheese; add a side salad or roasted veg instead.   - Ask the kitchen to box half before you start or portion off a serving.  Chinese - Pick steamed/grilled proteins or stir-fries with lots of vegetables (chicken, shrimp, lean pork, tofu).   - Ask for sauces on the side and \u201clight oil/no added salt.\u201d Favor ginger, hoisin, plum or bean-style sauces.   - Choose steamed or boiled rice (or half a portion) instead of egg fried rice; avoid prawn crackers and heavy fried starters.   - Better starters: clear broth soup, steamed vegetables, or a simple salad. Use chopsticks to slow eating.  Portable protein snack for work (easy) - Cooked chicken breast slices or canned tuna + a few whole-grain crackers and cherry tomatoes.   - Or 2 hard\u2011boiled eggs + a small handful of almonds \u2014 portable, filling, and high in protein.",
