      {
        "turn": 5,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "This is exactly the sort of advice I needed! Going to try those combos. \n\nI\u2019ve heard a lot about \u201cmental health\u201d being tied to lifestyle too. What are some practical steps for better psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a have better psychological health?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Nice \u2014 glad it helps! Here are simple, practical lifestyle steps you can start this week to boost your mental health:  - Move daily: keep your 20\u201330 min walk or micro\u2011workouts \u2014 activity reliably improves mood.   - Prioritize sleep: aim for consistent bed/wake times, finish eating 2\u20133 hours before bed, and cut screens 30\u201360 min before lights out.   - Brief mindfulness: 5 minutes of breathing or a short guided meditation each day (box breath: inhale 4s, hold 4s, exhale 4s).   - Small wins: set one tiny daily goal (make a healthy dinner, tidy your desk 10\u201315 min) and check it off.   - Gratitude/journaling: nightly list of 2\u20133 things you\u2019re grateful for or one positive moment from the day.   - Social connection: schedule one short check\u2011in a week with a friend or colleague.   - Food and routine: keep protein + veggies at meals, hydrate, limit alcohol and excess caffeine.   - Nature and breaks: get outside for even 10 minutes midday.   - Ask for help if needed: if low mood or anxiety persist or affect daily life, reach out to a GP or mental\u2011health professional.  Small, consistent changes compound \u2014 combine a few and build gradually.",
