            "clueweb22-en0020-29-18637:3": -3.988724708557129,
            "clueweb22-en0013-58-14941:0": -4.316354274749756
          },
          "ptkb_provenance": []
        }
      },
      {
        "turn": 7,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Love these! I usually do like to add veggies anyway. What\u2019s a good habit for reducing how much time I spend on my phone each night?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to lose weight?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 0,
          "text": "Nice \u2014 concrete, doable habits work best. Try this simple plan:  1) Set a nightly phone curfew: start with 30 minutes before bed for one week, then 60 minutes. Put the phone in another room to charge and enable Do Not Disturb/Bedtime mode.   2) Replace the habit: have a ready alternative (read a Stephen King chapter, do 3D\u2011printing prep, breathe/meditate, or a short walk). Swap one nightly doomscroll session for one of these.   3) Remove friction: hide social apps from your home screen, enable app limits or grayscale, and turn off nonessential notifications.   4) Make it social/accountable: tell a friend or household member you\u2019re doing a phone\u2011free hour and check in, or do an evening call instead of scrolling.   5) Use a physical alarm clock so you don\u2019t need the phone in the bedroom.  Small, consistent steps beat all\u2011or\u2011nothing. Build gradually and celebrate each phone\u2011free evening.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0013-25-16998:5": -3.3241891860961914,
