    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 1,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "I'm trying to figure out how to get started with a healthier and more active lifestyle. Any simple tips?",
          "user_rubrik": "How to get started to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Nice \u2014 small, consistent changes work best. Try this starter plan:  - Move first: aim for 20\u201330 minutes daily (walking, a 15\u2011min no\u2011equipment routine, or short strength sessions). Short daily workouts help energy and curb overeating.   - Add strength + protein: include a protein source at every meal (eggs, Greek yogurt, cottage cheese, legumes, tofu, tempeh, chicken or fish). A rule of thumb is ~20\u201330 g protein/meal to support muscle and satiety.   - Eat smarter out and late: when dining out, pick grilled/lean proteins, veggies, and ask for dressings on the side. If you eat late, keep portions moderate and add protein + fiber to avoid late bingeing; a short walk after dinner helps digestion.   - Lower CO2 impact: go flexitarian \u2014 more plants, fewer red\u2011meat meals. Legumes and tofu are high\u2011protein, low\u2011emissions swaps.   - Fix screen time & habits: schedule phone\u2011free windows (meals, 1 hour before bed). Replace doomscrolling with reading, 3D\u2011printing time, or social activities.   - Keep it realistic: set small goals, track progress, and workout with friends for accountability.",
