    "responses": [
      {
        "turn": 2,
        "response": {
          "rank": 1,
          "user_utterance": "Thanks, these are helpful! Got any tips on making late dinners healthier, especially since I often get home late from work?",
          "user_rubrik": "What are some practical steps to have a healthier and more active lifestyle?",
          "user_rubrik_score": 5,
          "text": "Great \u2014 practical, late-friendly tips:  - Smart pre-snack: if you get home very late, a small 100\u2013150 kcal nutrient-dense snack earlier (Greek yogurt, a small handful of nuts + a few pomegranate arils, or a piece of fruit) prevents overeating later.   - Build dinners around protein + fiber: aim for protein (tofu, tempeh, legumes, chicken, fish, cottage cheese) + veggies and a whole grain or sweet potato. These keep you full and help blood sugar.   - Split meals around workouts: if you exercise after work, eat a carb-focused half before working out and finish with protein + veggies after.   - Quick, low-effort meals: burrito bowls, shakshuka, or slow-cooker recipes you prep in the morning are ready when you get home. Add mango or berries for a satisfying dessert.   - Timing & digestion: avoid very large meals right before bed; try a short walk after dinner to aid digestion and sleep.   - Lower CO2: prefer legumes, tofu and plant-forward plates most nights.  Small, consistent swaps like these make late dinners healthier without huge effort.",
