          "text": "Nice \u2014 here are a few spices shown to support metabolism, with quick, practical ways to use them:  - Ginger \u2014 contains gingerol; try fresh grated in smoothies, stir\u2011fries, tea, or with roasted veggies.   - Turmeric \u2014 curcumin is the active compound; add to curries, roasted cauliflower, golden milk, or savory bowls.   - Black pepper \u2014 piperine may help limit formation of new fat cells; use as a regular finish seasoning on cooked meals.   - Cinnamon \u2014 supports thermogenesis; sprinkle on Greek yogurt, oatmeal, roasted sweet potato, or fruit (mango + cinnamon is tasty).   - Ginseng berry \u2014 contains ginsenosides with metabolic effects; usually consumed as a supplement/tea rather than a cooking spice.  Tip: use these as modest daily additions (teas, spice rubs, smoothies, roasted veggies). If you take meds or have health conditions, check with your clinician before starting concentrated supplements like ginseng.",
          "citations": {
            "clueweb22-en0020-77-15440:2": -0.84222412109375,
